FILE scratchpad/effected/jsonl/internal/tail.ts
6:// The bounded tail read.
7://
8:// `latest` and every `lastValid`-backed read go through this: `Line.lastValid`
9:// takes whole text, so "just read the file" is the easy wrong move — it makes
10:// the cost of answering "what is the current state" grow with the age of the
11:// journal, which is the thing this package exists to avoid.
12://
13:// Historical reads capture an absolute range, open the journal once, and read
14:// every bounded page of that range through `readSampledWindow` on the one
15:// handle. Growth past the sampled end is never read, a replacement after the
16:// sample cannot reach the pinned handle, and a page shorter than the sampled
17:// range fails `JournalResync` instead of ending the read early.
