goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:494:| 2026-10-06 | Treat the later #1468 fork-creation review as P1 correctness despite its P2 label and fix it in this wave. | The REST lookup now uses the pushed fork owner, but REST creation still submitted a bare branch to the upstream repository. With a same-named upstream branch, GitHub could open a PR from the wrong source; otherwise it could return 422. Creation now sends `head=<push owner>:<branch>`, using the same origin push-owner derivation. The fork draft regression asserts the exact POST field; 42 related Node/Bun tests, test-project typecheck, and Biome pass. The earlier full package run was stopped when source changed; current-head package and hosted proof remain separate. | Revert the qualified create head only if GitHub changes the REST field contract; replace it with a verified fork-safe field and rerun the fork regression before dropping the qualified owner. The previous bare head must not be restored without proving the upstream cannot select a same-named branch. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:500:| 2026-10-06 | Cancel the queued Heavy Admit run on draft PR #1468 so coverage-repair PRs #1452 and #1466 can take the runners first. Keep its tier-one checks running. | #1468 was pushed at `961c036396` with Yeet cheap gates green, but its main base does not yet include the two inherited coverage repairs. Heavy Admit run `37432107203` was queued and the branch must re-merge main and rerun hosted checks after those fixes land. The exact queued run was canceled through GitHub REST. | After both repairs merge, integrate `origin/main` once into #1468 and let the new head run Heavy. If the repairs are withdrawn, re-dispatch Heavy on #1468 after documenting the expected inherited coverage red. |
