1927:## Enforcement And Migration Posture
1929:This document defines the architecture. Repo checks, lint rules, package
1930:constraints, codemods, repo-cli commands, and generators are downstream
1931:mechanisms that must obey it.
1933:Architecture rules use four enforcement lanes:
1935:| Lane | Meaning |
1936:|------|---------|
1937:| `Doctrine` | Binding architecture rule or concept. |
1938:| `Generated Default` | Future generators/scaffolds should make this the default. |
1939:| `Review Gate` | Requires review evidence because the rule is contextual or exception-based. |
1940:| `Hard Check` | Should be enforced by lint, package metadata, import-boundary checks, fixture checks, or similar automation. |
1942:High-risk rules get an explicit lane and current status:
1944:| Rule area | Target lane | Current status | Future automation target |
1945:|-----------|-------------|----------------|--------------------------|
1946:| Shared promotion records | `Review Gate` | Docs-only package README requirement | Promotion metadata or README template checks |
1947:| `foundation/capability` routing | `Doctrine` + `Review Gate` | Docs-only negative gate and proof | Package metadata and dependency-boundary checks |
1948:| Package creation gates | `Doctrine` + `Generated Default` | Docs-only rule | Generator prompts and package metadata checks |
1949:| Canonical subpath names and browser roots | `Hard Check` | Target doctrine with transitional roots allowed | Export-map and import-boundary checks |
1950:| App Layer boundaries | `Doctrine` + `Review Gate` | Docs-only ownership test | No private reach-through imports from app runtime helpers |
1951:| Migration posture | `Doctrine` | Docs-only taxonomy | Repo-check reporting by bucket |
1952:| Browser capability routing | `Doctrine` + future `Hard Check` | Docs-only routing table | Browser-root and driver-root import checks |
1954:The migration posture has five buckets:
1956:| Bucket | Meaning |
1957:|--------|---------|
1958:| `Target Doctrine` | The architecture shape new work should follow. |
1959:| `Transitional Compatibility` | Existing shapes tolerated only to keep migration moving. |
1960:| `Cleanup-On-Touch` | Shapes that need not trigger a sweep, but must be cleaned when their boundary is edited. |
1961:| `Forbidden In New Work` | Shapes architecture-sensitive new work must not introduce. |
1962:| `Pending Automation/Generator Support` | Target shapes that should not trigger broad manual sweeps until tooling makes them repeatable. |
1964:New architecture-sensitive work must not introduce legacy labels as homes,
1965:package-root or `./*` wildcard exports as the canonical boundary contract,
1966:global runtime/config aggregation, direct env reads in slice code, or
1967:symmetry-only packages.
1969:Cleanup-on-touch is triggered by boundary edits: package manifests, exports,
1970:boundary-sensitive imports, ownership docs, config/shared/Layer surfaces, and
1971:architecture examples. Clean the touched boundary and adjacent docs/tests needed
1972:to keep that boundary honest; do not require whole-package or whole-family
1973:migration by default.
