FILE .patterns/testing-patterns.md
1:# Testing Patterns - Effect Library
3:## 🎯 OVERVIEW
5:Comprehensive testing strategies for the Effect library using @effect/vitest, with emphasis on proper Effect patterns, TestClock usage, and type-safe testing approaches.
7:## 🚨 CRITICAL TESTING REQUIREMENTS
9:### Testing Framework Selection
11:#### ✅ Use @effect/vitest for Effect-based modules
25:#### ✅ Use regular vitest for pure TypeScript functions
37:### ❌ FORBIDDEN PATTERNS
39:#### Never use Effect.runSync in tests
62:### Choose assertions by value, not by tester
64:`expect` and plain-value `assert` are legal inside `it.effect`. For Option,
65:Result, and Exit values, use the public `@effect/vitest/utils` helpers instead
66:of tag predicates or equality checks on the container. Keep both the expected
67:variant and its payload in the assertion; see the complete examples below.
82:## 🕐 TIME-DEPENDENT TESTING WITH TESTCLOCK
84:### ⚠️ CRITICAL: Always use TestClock for time-dependent operations
86:Any code that involves timing must use TestClock to avoid flaky tests:
148:### Operations requiring TestClock
150:- `Effect.sleep()` and `Effect.delay()`
151:- `Effect.timeout()` and `Effect.race()` with timeouts
152:- Scheduled operations and retry logic
153:- Queue operations with time-based completion
154:- Any concurrent operations dependent on timing
