131:### 1.2 `it.layer` semantics at rc.113
133:The pinned graph records current source ranges. Each block caches one built
134:Layer context and closes its shared scope once. Each inner Effect test still
135:runs under its own scoped body with that context. Nested blocks fork the parent
136:memo map and reuse outer instances.
138:Named blocks acquire in beforeAll and release in afterAll. Anonymous blocks
139:collect their non-skipped tasks, acquire through filtered beforeEach hooks and
140:release after the last task through onTestFinished, with afterAll as a cleanup
141:fallback. Shared-layer cleanup does not inherit the last test's aborted signal.
142:Hook acquisition timeout and body timeout are separate limits.
144:TestClock and TestConsole are shared across the block unless test services are
145:excluded. Time advanced by one test remains visible to later tests. Plain
146:it.effect provides fresh test services per test; it.live supplies none.
147:Named layer suites accept a concurrent option, including nested overrides.
148:Anonymous layers inherit their enclosing suite's concurrency. Use ctx.expect
149:for concurrent assertion counts and snapshots; concurrency does not isolate
150:shared resources or the shared TestClock.
152:Per-test Effect.provide(layer) still builds into a fresh scope per run. Expensive
153:containers, temporary resources and servers therefore need the shared-layer
154:judgment specified by D14. Cheap pure stubs remain exempt.
156:### 1.3 `it.prop` at rc.113
158:Sync it.prop, it.effect.prop and it.live.prop all accept tuple or record inputs
159:containing Schemas or native Arbitrary values from effect/unstable/arbitrary.
160:FastCheck Arbitraries and the old fastCheck option are unsupported. The option
161:is arbitrary: Arbitrary.CheckOptions, with runs, seed, replay, size, maxDiscards
162:and maxShrinks. Preserve generator constraints and failure/shrinking semantics
163:when translating older tests; this is more than a field rename.
165:Use `{ arbitrary: fcRuns(n) }` for explicit repository run floors. The current
166:@beep/fc-runs helper returns native runs/seed options and honors BEEP_FC_NUM_RUNS
167:and BEEP_FC_SEED. Native Arbitrary has no global configuration, so omitting the
168:option does not inherit the CI floor. PR properties must retain the 400-run
169:floor and seed 20260708; nightly retains its higher floor.
171:Callbacks receive generated values and TestContext. Effect/live callbacks return
172:Effect; synchronous callbacks must not return Effect or Promise. Returning false,
173:throwing or failing an Effect falsifies the property and triggers shrinking;
174:normal non-false completion passes. The test abort signal cancels generation,
175:evaluation and shrinking. Synchronous JavaScript that never returns cannot be
176:preempted. The instrumented runner must keep one lifecycle and one absolute
177:watchdog deadline across the complete property registration, including shrinking.
