320:## 5. Artifact schemas (author as `S.Class` in the lint command; JSONL rows are encoded forms)
322:### 5.1 Finding row (`EffectVitestFinding`)
344:### 5.2 Package digest (`ops/inventory/digests/<package>.md`)
346:Sections: totals per lens and severity; top 10 files by row count; the package's layer topology
347:(which shared resources exist, which are rebuilt per test today); MemoryFileSystem candidates;
348:flake history for the package (hosted failures in the last 30 days, from `gh run` / lane
349:timings); recommended wave order inside the package.
351:### 5.3 KG entry (`EffectVitestPrimitive`)
367:### 5.4 Timing summary (`ops/inventory/timings/{baseline,after}/<package>.json`)
369:`{ package, runner: "node-vitest", capturedAt, totalMs, testCount, files: [{ file, ms, tests }],
370:slowest: [{ file, testName, ms }] }` derived from the vitest JSON reporter output.
372:## 6. Lens charters (compact; expand into `ops/prompts/*.md` in P0e)
374:### 6.1 Resource & Dependency Authoritarian (owns D8, D14; P2 scope step)
376:Rules: share the expensive outer resource through `it.layer`, keep the per-test inner resource
377:scoped to the test body (`fs.makeTempDirectoryScoped()`, a fresh connection, a distinct table);
378:remove redundant whole-body `Effect.scoped` inside `it.effect` / `it.live` (the runner owns
379:that scope), while preserving deliberate shorter lifetimes for review; every
380:`withXyz` wrapper is deleted in favor of `it.layer` + scoped resources or `MemoryFileSystem`;
381:`{ timeout: "30 seconds" }` on container / server layers; nested `it.layer` for sub-dependencies;
382:SQL fixtures go through `makeSqlTestLayer` inside `it.layer`; `provideScopedLayer` call sites are
383:audited (most become `it.layer`). Gotchas to enforce: TestClock persists across a block. Choose
384:clock ownership and concurrency explicitly; do not reset a shared clock while another test uses
385:it. `excludeTestServices: true` removes TestClock and requires explicit provision when needed.
386:`Layer` values are memoized by identity inside a block, so a shared `MemoryFileSystem.layer` is one volume (make a
387:fresh layer per block when isolation matters); an `it.layer` build failure dies the whole block
388:(`Effect.orDie`), which is desired.
390:Canonical shape:
407:### 6.2 Flake Detective (owns D6; P2 flake step)
409:Attribute before touching: did the commit touch the package, did the job pass on an earlier run of
410:the branch, what is the local duration vs the CI timeout. Known repo classes: wall-clock polling of
411:an Atom registry (fixed in #975 by subscribing; TestClock cannot drive the detached registry
412:scheduler, so such tests are `it.live` with a named `Effect.timeoutOrElse`), `Effect.sleep` or a
413:`Schedule` under `it.effect` with no `TestClock.adjust` (hangs until the vitest timeout), unseeded
414:property tests surfacing latent bugs, EPIPE teardown in spawned writers, suite-order coverage arms,
415:container startup exceeding the hook timeout. Evidence sources: `gh run list` / `gh run view`,
416:`bun run beep ci lane-timings --runs 30`, the hosted job logs
417:(`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/jobs/<id>/logs`). `it.flakyTest` only per D6, always with a
418:`reason` row and a follow-up issue.
420:### 6.3 Property Tester (P2 property step)
422:Use production Schemas with it.prop for synchronous laws or it.effect.prop for
423:Effect-returning laws. Migrate direct legacy or native arbitrary checks into
424:these registrations with `{ arbitrary: fcRuns(n) }`, preserving seeds, floors,
425:replay and domain coverage. When a generated value crosses an invalid production
426:boundary, sharpen that production schema or its native arbitrary annotation.
427:Do not substitute a weaker test-only schema. Bound recursive generators and
428:collections with valid domain constraints instead of reducing trials or raising
429:timeouts. Reuse assertSchemaArbitraryDecodesToSelf for round-trip laws where it
430:fits. Reproduce the CI floor and seed with BEEP_FC_NUM_RUNS=400 and
431:BEEP_FC_SEED=20260708.
433:### 6.4 All Seeing Eye (owns D7; P2 observability step)
435:Design the instrumented it in @beep/test-utils using public APIs. Preserve the
436:complete tester surface, named/anonymous/nested layer callbacks and their
437:TestEnv behavior. Record start, end, duration, outcome and last observed log
438:through Effect logging, enabled only by BEEP_TEST_TRACE=1 or CI. Preserve user
439:loggers, test-console behavior, failures, interruption and finalizers.
441:Use a live-clock watchdog that beats the resolved Vitest task timeout. Use
442:TestClock.withLive only when TestClock is installed; live and excluded-test-service
443:modes need the actual live clock without that assumption. Do not advance virtual
444:time or change global limits. Each property registration shares one absolute
445:deadline across setup, trials and shrinking, with isolated state for overlapping
446:registrations. A layer acquisition timeout does not determine the body deadline.
447:Disabled timeouts require explicit handling. Validate every public integration
448:seam against the tag and installed runtime. P1/P2 timing evidence comes from the
449:Node Vitest JSON reporter, not instrumentation duration.
